      "text": "Statement:\n  The decomposition m_ij = mu + a_i + b_j + h_ij is unique under the zero-mean restrictions.\n\nOrthogonality under P_I P_J:\n  <a,b> = 0,  <a,h> = 0,  <b,h> = 0,\n  and the constant is orthogonal to all mean-zero components.\n\nWhy this matters:\n  Once the schedule is projected into (a,b,h), firm dispersion and assignment can be written as variance/covariance identities with no residual cross terms under product weights.",
